---
name: form-validation
description: Form/input validation testing template — required fields, format rules, boundaries
keywords: [form, validation, input, field, required, format, boundary, 表单, 验证]
---

## Applicable Scenarios
- Web forms with input validation
- API request validation
- User profile / registration forms

## Recommended Scenarios
1. **Required fields** — submitting empty required fields shows validation errors
2. **Format validation** — invalid email/phone/URL format rejected
3. **Boundary values** — minimum/maximum length for text fields
4. **Character restrictions** — special characters, XSS attempts
5. **Duplicate values** — submitting an already-taken username/email
6. **Field combinations** — dependent field validation (e.g. password confirmation match)

## Suggested Tags
@validation @form @negative @edge

## Common Step Patterns
- Given I am on the <form_name> form
- Given the <field> field is required
- When I submit with empty required fields
- When I enter "<value>" into the <field> field
- Then I should see a validation error for "<field>"
- Then the form should not be submitted
- Then I should see the error message "<message>"
